From: Felix Fietkau <nbd@nbd.name>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] MLD STA: restart the OBSS scan at a move of the association
 link

After a removal of the association link, the driver names another link
as the association link, and wpas_link_reconfig() reads it into
mlo_assoc_link_id. The OBSS scan keeps the setup that
sme_sched_obss_scan() made for the BSS of the old association link. If
the new association link is not on 2.4 GHz, the OBSS scan timer keeps
running, and each OBSS scan result makes the station send a 20/40 BSS
Coexistence frame to the AP of the new association link.

wpas_link_reconfig() updates current_bss only where the BSSID from the
driver changes. With the SME in wpa_supplicant, that BSSID is the AP MLD
address, which stays the same at the move.

Where the association link changes, take the BSS of the new association
link as current_bss, signal the change of CurrentBSS and set up the OBSS
scan again. sme_sched_obss_scan() stops the timer, ignores the result of
a scan in progress, and starts the timer again only for a BSS on 2.4 GHz
that supports HT40 and asks for OBSS scans. Without a BSS entry for the
new association link, the OBSS scan stops. The OBSS scan runs while
new_connection is 0: wpa_supplicant_set_state() starts it when it clears
new_connection at WPA_COMPLETED, and stops it when it sets
new_connection again.

Signed-off-by: Felix Fietkau <nbd@nbd.name>
---
--- a/wpa_supplicant/events.c
+++ b/wpa_supplicant/events.c
@@ -6773,6 +6773,7 @@ static void wpas_removed_links_forget(st
 static void wpas_link_reconfig(struct wpa_supplicant *wpa_s)
 {
 	u16 old_links = wpa_s->valid_links;
+	u8 old_assoc_link_id = wpa_s->mlo_assoc_link_id;
 	u8 bssid[ETH_ALEN];
 
 	if (wpa_drv_get_bssid(wpa_s, bssid) < 0) {
@@ -6808,6 +6809,16 @@ static void wpas_link_reconfig(struct wp
 	    wpa_s->links[wpa_s->mlo_assoc_link_id].freq)
 		wpa_s->assoc_freq = wpa_s->links[wpa_s->mlo_assoc_link_id].freq;
 
+	if (wpa_s->mlo_assoc_link_id != old_assoc_link_id) {
+		struct wpa_bss *bss = wpa_supplicant_update_current_bss(
+			wpa_s, wpa_s->links[wpa_s->mlo_assoc_link_id].bssid);
+
+		if (bss)
+			wpas_notify_bssid_changed(wpa_s);
+		/* The OBSS scan runs while new_connection is 0 */
+		sme_sched_obss_scan(wpa_s, bss && !wpa_s->new_connection);
+	}
+
 	/* The BSS of a link the station deleted itself stays on air */
 	wpas_removed_links_forget(wpa_s, old_links & ~wpa_s->valid_links &
 				  ~wpa_s->requested_link_deletes);
